her for longer", "at": 1792254435, "direction": 1, "url": "", "nodes": ["Interest_Rates"]}, "rows": 1, "ms": 1.2}, {"name": "CREATE_ALERT", "cypher": "MATCH (e:Event {id: $event_id}) CREATE (al:Alert {id: $id, text: $text, at: $at, answer_type: $answer_type})-[:FROM]->(e) WITH al UNWIND $tickers AS t MATCH (a:Asset {ticker: t}) CREATE (al)-[:FLAGS]->(a) RETURN al.id AS id", "params": {"id": "alr_8f8d8c6c38", "event_id": "evt_0bf9316a2a", "text": "Higher-for-longer rates strongly pressure homebuilders, retail banks, credit and commercial real estate within ~3 months; brokers holding cash (IBKR, SCHW) benefit. Knock-on: stronger dollar weighs on copper; data center buildout slows, then electrical equipment over ~12 months.", "at": 1792254435, "answer_type": "answered", "tickers": ["DHI", "LEN", "TOL", "WFC", "IBKR", "SCHW"]}, "rows": 6, "ms": 1.42}]}, {"type": "brief", "answer_type": "answered", "text": "Borrowing costs staying high most likely hurt homebuilders like DHI, LEN and TOL, with banks like WFC also squeezed.\n\nThe most surprising effect is on copper: higher interest rates, then a stronger dollar, then a moderate drop in copper prices within about a month. Online brokers such as IBKR and SCHW come out ahead because they earn more on the cash their customers hold. The hit to housing is strong and should show within about 3 months, while slower data center building then means weaker demand for electrical equipment over about a year.", "analysis": {"sources": ["Interest_Rates"], "direction": 1, "depth": 4, "drivers": [{"id": "Interest_Rates", "impact": 1.0, "direction": 1, "hops": 0, "lag_months": 0, "path": ["Interest_Rates"]}, {"id": "Housing_and_Homebuilders", "impact": 0.996, "direction": -1, "hops": 1, "lag_months": 3, "path": ["Interest_Rates", "Housing_and_Homebuilders"]}, {"id": "Retail_Banking", "impact": 0.691, "direction": -1, "hops": 1, "lag_months": 3, "path": ["Interest_Rates", "Retail_Banking"]}, {"id": "Credit_Conditions", "impact": 0.615, "dir